      <data key="d7">The #Palisadian-Post Prints Its Last Edition. Its final online issue is up now. The Palisadian-Post was published for 97 years, but the twice-monthly community #newspaper couldn’t survive the Los Angeles "wildfires. "…Alan Smolinisky, the owner of the paper, said that the #Palisades became a “ghost town” after the fire, bringing readership effectively down to zero." “We lost the one thing we can’t do without — our readers,” he wrote. #PalisadesFire 🎁 https://www.nytimes.com/2025/12/14/us/califo…</data>
