      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">From the article: "...The biggest culprit, she said, was the message that echoed all over the county: It referenced a fire “in your area” without specifying a location and did not reference a time. The confusion the message stoked as it echoed throughout the county over the next 24 hours could have been avoided, Sutton said, if it contained more precise information. “An EVACUATION WARNING has been issued for Calabasas/Agoura Hills,” for example, instead of “An EVACUATION WARNING has been issued…</data>
