      <data key="d5">2025-01-17T03:54:17.000Z</data>
      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">@jeridansky @ai6yr Doesn't look like there is an effective option. Common residential washing machines won't get them properly cleaned - and could taint the next load(s). Put in tightly sealed plastic bag and dispose of properly. https://enviroliteracy.org/can-asbestos-be-washed-out-of-clothes/</data>
