    <node id="113841797387892738">
      <data key="d2">@JohnJBurnsIII@kzoo.to: @jeridansky @ai6yr Pretty sure the remediators use the sealed Tyvek s…</data>
      <data key="d3">109679802491186088</data>
      <data key="d4">JohnJBurnsIII@kzoo.to</data>
      <data key="d5">2025-01-17T04:26:11.000Z</data>
      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">@jeridansky @ai6yr Pretty sure the remediators use the sealed Tyvek suits - taped joints and all of that is stripped off and goes into bags... and then they go into contamination showers... So all of us "normal folks" would not have that type of system... Additionally - if your own house is not well sealed - and houses with those bad things are burning around you --- your house could be contaminated. Yourself, your vehicles, etc. --- There is nothing good coming out of those fires.</data>
