    <node id="113841812097114155">
      <data key="d2">@ai6yr@m.ai6yr.org: @JohnJBurnsIII @jeridansky Various friends we know (Thomas Fire, Wool…</data>
      <data key="d3">109321601315889133</data>
      <data key="d4">ai6yr@m.ai6yr.org</data>
      <data key="d5">2025-01-17T04:29:55.000Z</data>
      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">@JohnJBurnsIII @jeridansky Various friends we know (Thomas Fire, Woolsey Fire) had to remove every single thing that was fabric out of their house and throw them away (due to that kind of contamination). Curtains, bedding, towels, books, all clothing, carpet. Walls and ceilings had to be washed, repainted. A lot of other stuff (even hard surfaced things but which absorbed smoke) -- were also a loss. Imagine the smell of anything from a smoking household... very few things escape. So, even if yo…</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">context_descendants</data>
