    <node id="113841841304212042">
      <data key="d2">@ai6yr@m.ai6yr.org: @JohnJBurnsIII @jeridansky They most certainly do, and they have spec…</data>
      <data key="d3">109321601315889133</data>
      <data key="d4">ai6yr@m.ai6yr.org</data>
      <data key="d5">2025-01-17T04:37:22.000Z</data>
      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">@JohnJBurnsIII @jeridansky They most certainly do, and they have special removal tents and stuff they swab to collect the fibers, plus air scrubbers (basically industrial Corsi Rosenthal boxes). I watched them do that for our kitchen, which is now entombed in a hazmat site... LOL... "We tested your kitchen tile, and it has lead, so we have to remediate it with a hazmat company" (as week or so later) "We removed your leaded kitchen tile, and underneath it is 70% asbestos tile, we need to remedia…</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">context_descendants</data>
