    <node id="113944018752383835">
      <data key="d2">@Kathmandu@stranger.social: @exador23 We saw that in the Colorado fires a year or two ago, also.…</data>
      <data key="d3">109752047061675651</data>
      <data key="d4">Kathmandu@stranger.social</data>
      <data key="d5">2025-02-04T05:42:26.000Z</data>
      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">@exador23 We saw that in the Colorado fires a year or two ago, also. Houses are built of dry wood; they burn to the ground. Trees are wet, living wood; they get singed a little. There were photographs of whole neighborhoods with every house reduced to cinders and all the trees still mostly intact. Trees are not our enemies.</data>
