    <node id="114501605342474251">
      <data key="d2">@meganL@mas.to: @BenAveling @ai6yr The way co-opping helps is creating insurance that…</data>
      <data key="d3">112170269206349103</data>
      <data key="d4">meganL@mas.to</data>
      <data key="d5">2025-05-13T17:04:02.000Z</data>
      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">@BenAveling @ai6yr The way co-opping helps is creating insurance that's oriented towards helping each other rather than paying top salaries to CEOs and fat dividends to shareholders. It's not that a co-op would never refuse to underwrite a policy...it's that they wouldn't underwrite and then refuse to pay out, which these insurance corporations do all the damned time. While expecting the taxpayer to pick up the slack. The public is better off providing directly for each other.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
