      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">@ai6yr Chicken vs egg question. The MI could have just been coincidental timing, but the associated hypoxia with the inhalation and based on that post you boosted the other day, chemicals in the smoke, reduced myocardial oxygen levels to the point the cells started dying and disrrhythmias associated with hypoxia was most likely the precipitating factor. Add to that the stress and anxiety of the event and you are in big trouble Interesting side note, normal myocardial cells have a typical action…</data>
