      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">@frank @MakerAndBakerDesigns There's no way to know how big a deal this may be. But the Aug 12, 2026 total solar eclipse falls on the day when the annual Perseids meteor shower is at its peak. Be alert for meteors, but aware the twilight may or may not be dim enough depending on how bright any random meteors are in the 4 minutes or less of totality.</data>
