      <data key="d3">117169473084457668</data>
      <data key="d4">Zelda@m.ai6yr.org</data>
      <data key="d5">2026-09-01T05:14:40.000Z</data>
      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">@ai6yr Insurance — any insurance — amounts to being a scam in the United States. You can pay all your dues on time, early, or upfront, and follow all the policy terms and conditions, but they'll still try to deny your claim. Then, either you fight it if you can, or they wait you out — possibly outspending you — just for you to get little or nothing in return. Assuming you win, they may appeal that indifferently or hold off payment seemingly indifferently too.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
