      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">@ai6yr I don’t know if you’ve noticed but Ryan Halls crew (mainly Andy I think) has started doing their own “y’all watch” zones for tornadoes. They do their own polygon - a different color than NWS- and explain that “based on x, y, z factors this is where we think the storm/tornado is heading” Sometimes they add “with a nn% probability” Not mentioning names… but too bad some other folks aren’t brave enough to do something similar for evac warnings 😗🤷🏻‍♀️</data>
