    <node id="113992328163224810">
      <data key="d2">@mappingsupport@m.ai6yr.org: @exador23 @ai6yr One thing that was learned from the 2018 Montecito #…</data>
      <data key="d3">110433002329275149</data>
      <data key="d4">mappingsupport@m.ai6yr.org</data>
      <data key="d5">2025-02-12T18:28:06.000Z</data>
      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">@exador23 @ai6yr One thing that was learned from the 2018 Montecito #DebrisFlow was that at bends in the channel the material sometimes tends to pile up and then overshoot the bank on the downward side. The debris flow then continues *outside* the channel by finding a new path of least resistance which could very well be right down streets, through yards, etc.</data>
      <data key="d8">debrisflow</data>
      <data key="d9">context_descendants</data>
      <data key="d10">1</data>
      <data key="d11">2</data>
      <data key="d12">4</data>
      <data key="d13">1</data>
      <data key="d14">0</data>
      <data key="d15">2</data>
      <data key="d16">1</data>
      <data key="d17">1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="113992458057999983">
      <data key="d2">@exador23@m.ai6yr.org: @mappingsupport @ai6yr Anywhere the flow would slow or go through a b…</data>
      <data key="d3">109366550461584397</data>
      <data key="d4">exador23@m.ai6yr.org</data>
      <data key="d5">2025-02-12T19:01:10.000Z</data>
      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">@mappingsupport @ai6yr Anywhere the flow would slow or go through a bottleneck too. Allows debris to settle out which then fills up the space and as additional material comes down it spills out in unexpected directions. Learned a LOT about flows from this lecture a couple weeks ago by caltech geologist Michael Lamb https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N5M9LlZhAIo first 12 minutes is just introduction stuff. The new (to me at least) science starts around the 30 minute point. Turns out the hydrophobic…</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">context_descendants</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">8</data>
      <data key="d12">9</data>
      <data key="d13">1</data>
      <data key="d14">0</data>
      <data key="d15">1</data>
      <data key="d16">1</data>
      <data key="d17">0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="113986251604944303">
      <data key="d2">@JTO_is_Typing@mstdn.games: To be clear, I'm not criticizing, and from the briefings alone the te…</data>
      <data key="d3">110875475891251931</data>
      <data key="d4">JTO_is_Typing@mstdn.games</data>
      <data key="d5">2025-02-11T16:42:48.000Z</data>
      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">To be clear, I'm not criticizing, and from the briefings alone the teams putting in these fortifications have done a record number in a record time and got there ahead of this coming storm. This one little error adds a bit of humor in these dark times.</data>
